# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EOL policy: LF in the index, LF on disk, on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists (the PIN-hash integrity story):
# src/i18n/ui-locale-bundles/ holds bundles vendored byte-for-byte from
# phlix-ui, SHA-256-pinned in the PIN manifest. tests/unit/i18nLocales.test.ts
# hashes the WORKING-TREE bytes of each vendored file against that pin.
# Git-for-Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so on a windows-latest CI
# checkout the LF blobs would be silently rewritten to CRLF on disk before
# hashing — the pin test would fail on Windows while ubuntu passes (the exact
# class fixed on the windows client by PR #46 / commit 0c6163d). The committed
# blobs are all LF; checkout conversion is the only threat.
#
# .gitattributes settings take precedence over core.autocrlf, so pinning the
# policy here makes the vendored bytes (and every other text file) identical
# on disk in every clone, dev machine, and CI shard — and keeps the PIN test
# strict (byte-exact) instead of forcing it to tolerate CRLF.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Treat files as text by content: normalize to LF on commit, check out as LF.
# Covers src/** (vendored bundles, catalogs, tests), package/** (committed
# dist assets), docs/**, *.md, JSON, lockfiles, YAML/XML, scripts — the whole
# estate-standard text surface.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never EOL-normalized on add or checkout (a converted font or
# icon is a corrupted one; `binary` also keeps them out of
# `git add --renormalize`). Extensions listed from this repo's actual tracked
# inventory (package/assets woff2 fonts, icon.png).
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
